description:
Turn a raw inbound HTTP request into the domain's validated Request at the web boundary. The PURE request rules are already done (gitweb_in_rust-evs: model/action.rs %actions table, model/request.rs query-param validation, model/path_info.rs evaluate_path_info decomposition). What is missing is the IMPURE boundary adapter that gitweb performs in evaluate_path_info plus the query/PATH_INFO merge:
- resolve which leading PATH_INFO component(s) name an existing project by walking projectroot (gitweb check_head_link), since project names can contain slashes;
- run PathInfo::parse on the remainder ONLY when the query string did not already pin an action;
- merge query parameters with PATH_INFO-derived fields under gitweb's precedence, then validate the whole into a Request;
- resolve the three still-deferred view-preference params (ds / by_tag / js).
Read gitweb's evaluate_path_info and evaluate_query_params before implementing. The domain stays untouched; this is a web-crate adapter over the ProjectStore/Repository ports and the done request rules.

ACCEPTANCE (features/web, over a gix-built projectroot fixture): project-prefix resolution for no project / a simple project / a nested slash-containing project / a non-existent prefix; query-pins-action suppresses PATH_INFO; the path supplies the action when the query does not; the query+PATH_INFO precedence merge; an unsafe or invalid field is rejected with the same status the domain rule yields.

Produce the effective gitweb configuration the rest of the app reads. The file SELECTION rule (which global files load and in what order: built-in < GITWEB_CONFIG_COMMON < GITWEB_CONFIG / GITWEB_CONFIG_SYSTEM) is DONE in model/config_chain.rs. This bead owns the rest of the global config story:
- the representation of the global settings gitweb-rs actually consumes (projectroot, site name, base/clone URLs, the ~20 %feature toggles, ...) -- scope it from gitweb's our-variable defaults and the %feature hash;
- a declarative on-disk format for the global config files: gitweb's are executable Perl and we will NOT run Perl, so choose a sane declarative format and document the gitweb-variable -> setting mapping;
- the pure precedence rule that resolves each setting across an ordered list of sources (built-in < COMMON < CONFIG/SYSTEM < per-project), respecting that gitweb settings compose differently (scalar replace vs list/array semantics vs feature toggles) -- model this as a domain rule with its own Gherkin (zero/one/many sources, each compose kind);
- the inbound loader that reads the files selected by config_chain into the resolved config.
Per-project gitweb.* values are already read by the git adapter (gitweb_in_rust-reh) and layer on top. Read gitweb's evaluate_gitweb_config, the %feature hash, and git_get_project_config.

ACCEPTANCE: domain Gherkin for the precedence rule; the loader verified against on-disk fixture config files producing the expected resolved settings.
